<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame illuminated">
    <p class="kicker">A proposed crossing map and a local χ-front</p>
    <h2 id="t-seam-equation">Where the Dot Would Live Mathematically</h2>
    <p>Introduce \(\xi\in(-1,0)\) as a <em>residue coordinate</em>, not an extra spatial direction that a
      telescope could point toward. Let \(r_-(\xi,y)\) describe whatever pattern survives on that branch.
      A seam kernel \(\mathcal K_{-+}\) would project it into source events in positive spacetime:</p>
    <p class="formula">\[
      J_+(x,t)=g\!\int_{-1}^{0}\!d\xi\int d\mu_-(y)\,
      \mathcal K_{-+}(x,t;\xi,y)\,r_-(\xi,y).
    \]</p>
    <p>This equation names the missing mechanism. The kernel must say <em>where</em> a residue can emerge,
      whether orientation is reversed, how locality is recovered, and why the events cluster in the young
      universe. Its coupling \(g\), measure \(d\mu_-\), dimensions and dynamics are all presently unknown.</p>
    <p>The inherited source could then enter a positive-side evolution law rather than replacing it:</p>
    <p class="formula">\[
      \frac{D\chi}{Dt}=F_{\rm TTI}[\chi,g_{\mu\nu},\rho,T]+J_+(x,t).
    \]</p>
    <p>Define the observable little-red-dot seam as the region where the local field is both intermediate and
      changing rapidly:</p>
    <p class="formula">\[
      \Sigma_{\rm LRD}(t)=
      \left\{x:\frac12&lt;\chi(x,t)&lt;1,
      \quad \frac{D\chi}{Dt}>0,
      \quad |\nabla\chi|>\chi_{\rm c}\right\}.
    \]</p>
    <p>The first condition places the region between the Ledger&rsquo;s middle and final states. The second says
      it is becoming more integrated rather than relaxing back toward the dark state. The third makes it a
      narrow front rather than an entire galaxy glowing uniformly.</p>
    <p>A phenomenological luminosity for the transition could then be written</p>
    <p class="formula">\[
      L_{\chi}=\epsilon_{\chi}
      \int_{\Sigma_{\rm LRD}}
      \rho c^2\,\max\!\left(\frac{D\chi}{Dt},0\right)dV,
    \]</p>
    <p>where \(\epsilon_{\chi}\) is the fraction of integration energy reaching radiation. The observed
      spectrum would still be this power plus ordinary accretion light after gas has absorbed, scattered and
      re-emitted it:</p>
    <p class="formula">\[
      L_{\lambda}^{\rm obs}
      =\mathcal T_{\lambda}(\rho,T,\tau)
      \left[L_{\lambda}^{\rm acc}+L_{\lambda}^{\chi}\right].
    \]</p>
    <h3 id="t-conservation">The conservation fork</h3>
    <p>If only <em>information or topology</em> crosses, \(J_+\) selects initial conditions but contributes no
      energy; the black hole and cocoon must be paid for entirely by matter already in this universe. If
      <em>mass-energy</em> crosses, the two branches require a balanced exchange current:</p>
    <p class="formula">\[
      \nabla_{\mu}T_{+}^{\mu\nu}=J_{-+}^{\nu},
      \qquad
      \nabla_{\mu}T_{-}^{\mu\nu}=-J_{-+}^{\nu},
      \qquad
      \Delta E_+ + \Delta E_-=0.
    \]</p>
    <p>The second option risks double counting: the inherited energy cannot also be ordinary accretion energy,
      and the negative label does not licence negative mass. A third, weaker possibility is that no substance
      crosses at all; the two sides merely satisfy one global junction condition. These alternatives lead to
      different observations and cannot be blended when convenient.</p>
    <p class="lede">These equations make the idea writable, not true.</p>
    <p>Neither \(\mathcal K_{-+}\), \(g\), \(\epsilon_{\chi}\), the threshold \(\chi_{\rm c}\), nor the
      evolution law for \(\chi\) has been derived from TTI&rsquo;s modified Einstein equations. If they can be
      tuned separately for every object, the proposal explains nothing. The debt is to derive them once and
      then let the sky refuse the result. <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap">
  <div class="page-head tight">
    <p class="kicker">Four parts of TTI meet at the dot</p>
    <h2 id="t-three-readings">Inheritance, Integration, Seam, and Torus</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="grid two">
    <div class="frame card illuminated">
      <h3>Inheritance</h3>
      <p>The \((-1,0)\) corridor supplies a proposed antecedent. It says why an exceptionally compact seed
        might already possess closure structure at cosmic dawn. It does not yet say whether the inheritance is
        energy, information or a junction condition. <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></p>
    </div>
    <div class="frame card">
      <h3>Integration</h3>
      <p>The <a href="/cosmic-ledger/#t-chi">\(\chi\)-field</a> supplies the positive-side move from partial
        to complete phase. The old residue, if real, initiates or biases that move; it does not replace the gas,
        gravity and local geometry that perform it. <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></p>
    </div>
    <div class="frame card">
      <h3>Seam</h3>
      <p>The <a href="/seams/#t-horizon">event horizon</a> is TTI&rsquo;s stellar-scale closure boundary. The
        stronger conjecture nests one seam inside another: a black-hole horizon on the positive side localises
        the deeper identification \(0^-\sim0^+\). <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></p>
    </div>
    <div class="frame card illuminated">
      <h3>Torus</h3>
      <p>Accreting material circulates while fields and outflows return through a larger loop. TTI reads that
        as its toroidal grammar, but ordinary accretion theory already explains the circulation. Shape alone
        is not evidence for inherited residue. <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

